# Technical Release Coordinator
  [button] Apply
  text: Job Title: Technical Release Coordinator
  text: The Technical Release Coordinator manages and coordinates technology releases across multiple teams and applications. This role owns release
  text: The Technical Release Coordinator partners with development teams, Scrum teams, infrastructure resources, project leaders, and business stak
  text: Coordinate regularly scheduled releases, out-of-cycle deployments, and emergency fixes across multiple teams.
  text: Facilitate release-planning meetings to determine scope, sequencing, timelines, dependencies, and deployment requirements.
  text: Develop and document release recommendations, including:
  text: Release scope and schedule
  text: Deliverables and component listings
  text: Testing and validation requirements
  text: Risk-mitigation and rollback plans
  text: Establish release-readiness criteria and track projects through the change-ticket lifecycle.
  text: Ensure change tickets are complete and include required testing documentation, implementation instructions, approvals, and rollback plans.
  text: Create and maintain the consolidated release calendar, configuration plan, deployment schedule, and stakeholder communications.
  text: Prepare for and participate in Change Advisory Board meetings, deployment-planning sessions, and implementation-readiness reviews.
  text: Identify scheduling conflicts, missing requirements, technical dependencies, and risks that could affect release outcomes.
  text: Direct off-hours release activities, including deployment coordination, status reporting, issue escalation, and resolution.
  text: Coordinate mock deployments, pre-production checklists, production implementation, and post-production verification.
  text: Compile and review deployment and validation instructions in partnership with development and technical teams.
  text: Package and stage production-ready release artifacts.
  text: Coordinate the provisioning and readiness of infrastructure resources and environments.
  text: Establish and enforce controls for build management, release management, and production change control.
  text: Provide input on code-branching and code-merge strategies to project delivery teams and IT stakeholders.
  text: Collaborate with technical resources to improve and automate build and deployment processes.
  text: Communicate release status, business impact, expected duration, issues, and outcomes before, during, and after deployments.
  text: Lead release-review meetings, capture lessons learned, and incorporate improvements into future releases.
  text: Maintain release templates, process documentation, procedures, and best practices.
  text: Promote continuous improvement across change, build, configuration, and release-management processes.
  text: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.
  text: More than five years of technology experience, including one to four years of relevant experience coordinating projects or software releases
  text: Experience managing releases of varying size, scope, complexity, and business impact.
  text: Knowledge of the software development lifecycle.
  text: Experience working with change management processes and production deployments.
  text: Hands-on software development experience using object-oriented programming concepts.
  text: Experience with code merges, branching strategies, build processes, and deployment activities.
  text: General understanding of Agile development practices.
  text: General understanding of ITIL practices.
  text: Ability to participate in scheduled off-hours, weekend, or emergency release activities.
  text: Experience coordinating releases in a complex enterprise environment.
  text: Familiarity with automated build and deployment processes, CI/CD pipelines, and release-management tools.
  text: Experience supporting Change Advisory Board processes and IT governance controls.
  text: Experience coordinating infrastructure or application-environment provisioning.
  text: Knowledge of configuration management, source control, and production validation practices.
  text: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities
  text: Strong planning, organization, and project-coordination skills.
  text: Ability to manage multiple releases, deadlines, and technical dependencies simultaneously.
  text: Strong risk-identification, problem-solving, and escalation skills.
  text: Ability to communicate technical release information clearly to technical and nontechnical stakeholders.
  text: Strong attention to detail and commitment to accurate documentation.
  text: Ability to influence teams and drive activities to completion without direct authority.
  text: Sound judgment when evaluating release readiness, risk, and production impact.
  text: Ability to remain composed and make timely decisions during high-impact deployments or production issues.
  text: Commitment to process improvement, operational stability, and high-quality release outcomes.
  text: Salary is commensurate to experience, location, etc.
  text: Horace Mann was founded in 1945 by two Springfield, Illinois, teachers who saw a need for quality, affordable auto insurance for teachers. S
  text: We’re motivated by the fact that educators take care of our children’s future, and we believe they deserve someone to look after theirs. We 
  text: EOE/Minorities/Females/Veterans/Disabled. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, 
